.TH IOWATCHD-NOTIFY 1 "October 2026" "iowatchd 0.5.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
iowatchd-notify \- desktop pop-up for iowatchd alerts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iowatchd-notify
.SH DESCRIPTION
Helper meant to be used as the \fBnotify_command\fR of \fBiowatchd\fR(8). It
shows a desktop pop-up with \fBnotify-send\fR(1) on the session bus of every
logged-in user, since iowatchd runs as root and has no desktop session itself.
It exits silently if \fBnotify-send\fR is not installed.
.PP
Alert pop-ups are limited to one per minute; recovery pop-ups are always
shown. The script reads the \fBIOWATCHD_*\fR variables set by iowatchd
(for example \fBIOWATCHD_EVENT\fR, \fBIOWATCHD_DEVICE\fR, \fBIOWATCHD_UTIL\fR
and \fBIOWATCHD_MESSAGE\fR).
.SH EXAMPLE
In \fI/etc/iowatchd.conf\fR:
.PP
.RS
notify_command = iowatchd-notify
.RE
.PP
then reload the service with \fBsystemctl reload iowatchd\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR iowatchd (8),
.BR iowatchd.conf (5)
